{
  // X: Beyond the Frontier's sector map. games/xtension has its own.
  //
  // name, xbtfTextId, x and y are the game's own: the text tables name every sector, and the text
  // id encodes its cell (2YX in XBTF; x runs east, y south, from 1).
  //
  // race and gates are not in any game file decoded so far (the universe is set up by the compiled
  // script, l/001.obj). They are read from elite-games.ru's map, xbtf.png, by sampling
  // each cell's colour and the midpoint of every shared edge, where a
  // wall is black background and a gate is not. Gates are symmetric; each lists the directions
  // it opens to.
  //
  // stations come from the same site's Excel map (mapxbtf.rar), which draws each sector as a
  // 16 x 16 block, top-down, with station codes where the stations stand. x and z are that
  // position in metres from the sector's centre (x east, z north) at 1.5 km per cell: the
  // sheet is a schematic, so the spacing is ours, chosen so no two stations' radii overlap.
  // Codes are read by the sector's race (N1 in an Argon sector is the wheat farm, in a Boron
  // one the plankton farm). Its unexplained markers (*, + and one V in an enemy sector) are
  // skipped. A station of another race inside a sector would be misread; the map gives no
  // way to tell.
  //
  // A mod changes the map by layering its own data/sectors/sectors.json; entries merge by id.
